# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-options — plug-in-defined CLI options with arguments; activation
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-loader
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

Sub-issue of =alfe-plugin-model=: "a plug-in can define CLI options with
arguments" (pjb, 2026-09-21). Replaces the built-in =--epure= spec and the
alfe-only =epure-p= slot of =clautolisp.autolisp-cli:cli-options=.

* Proposal

- Option kinds: =:flag= (no argument), =:value= (one argument; =--opt V= and
  =--opt=V=), repeatable variants (accumulate a list), optional =:parser=
  (string → value, signals =cli-usage-error=), =:choices=, =:env= (default
  from an environment variable) and =:default=. Resolution order: command
  line, then environment, then default — done once, right after parsing.
- *Namespacing rule:* a plug-in =NAME= may define only =--NAME= and
  =--NAME-…=; no short options; a collision with a core option or another
  plug-in's option is a registration error.
- *Activation.* A plug-in is active when its activation flag is given (or
  its env default is truthy), or =--plugin NAME=, or it is named in
  =$ALFE_PLUGINS=. A plug-in option given while its plug-in is inactive is
  a usage error naming the flag to add.
- =cli-options= gains =plugin-options= (alist plug-in name → plist of
  resolved values) and =plugins-active= (names, activation order);
  =epure-p= goes away. =*AUTOLISP-PLUGIN-OPTIONS*= becomes the list of
  symbols naming the active plug-ins (=(EPURE)= for =--epure=, as before).
- =--help= gains a "Plug-in options" section generated from the registered
  options (installed plug-ins, whether or not active), and =--plugin NAME=.
- The removed built-in =--epure= keeps working: the EPURE plug-in defines it.

* Acceptance criteria

- Unit tests: parsing each option kind, env/default precedence, the
  namespacing rule, collisions, activation and the "requires" error.
- =tests/scenarios/cli/dwg-and-epure.sexp= and the option-coverage scenario
  pass with =--epure= supplied by the plug-in.
- =--help= lists plug-in options; the man page and user manual agree.
